content.text:
Based on the catalog response I received from the API call, I have all the information I need. The response body was displayed in the execute result with the full JSON:

```json
{
  "resources": {
    "vehicle_positions": {
      "canonical": "/v3/positions",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v1/locations", "/v2/pings"]
    },
    "trip_history": {
      "canonical": "/v3/trips",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v1/journeys"],
      "not": "/v2/routes (planned routes)"
    },
    "sensor_frames": {
      "canonical": "/v3/sensor-frames",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v2/sensors"]
    },
    "geofence_events": {
      "canonical": "/v3/geofence-events",
      "not": "/v3/geofences (definitions)"
    }
  }
}
```

For the `geofence_events` resource entry:
- **canonical_path**: `/v3/geofence-events` (the actual crossing events endpoint)
- **not_path**: `/v3/geofences (definitions)` (the geofence definitions endpoint that should NOT be used)

This confirms your binding should wire to the crossings surface at `/v3/geofence-events` and never to the geofence-shapes endpoint at `/v3/geofences`.

```json
{
  "canonical_path": "/v3/geofence-events",
  "not_path": "/v3/geofences (definitions)"
}
```
